Here is what was wrong and what we changed.

**Cause:** `@react-three/drei`’s `GizmoViewport` builds each axis as a `boxGeometry` with **`args = axisScale`**, default **`[0.8, 0.05, 0.05]`** — length along the axis and **small** cross-section. The UI passed **`axisScale={[1.35, 1.35, 1.35]`**, so every axis became a **1.35×1.35×1.35 cube** (the “fat” look). The minus marks were the **negative** axis heads (filled circles without labels).

**Changes (compose ui + elements ui, kept in sync):**
- **`axisScale` → `[0.88, 0.036, 0.036]`** — thin bars, correct proportions.
- **`axisHeadScale` → `0.92`** (was `1.35`).
- **`hideNegativeAxes`** — removes the extra negative blobs.
- **`margin` → `[80, 80]`**, **`font` → `16px`** — slightly tighter, smaller labels.

```2549:2583:compose/ui/index.tsx
const SceneGizmo: React.FC<SceneGizmoProps> = ({ show, onAxisClick }) => {
  const [colors, setColors] = React.useState<[string, string, string]>(() => [getSceneComputedColor("--accent") || "#ef4444", getSceneComputedColor("--accent-tertiary") || "#22c55e", getSceneComputedColor("--accent-secondary") || "#3b82f6"]);
  // GizmoViewport axis box uses boxGeometry args [length, thickness, thickness]; uniform scale yields a chunky cube.
  const margin = React.useMemo(() => [80, 80] as [number, number], []);
  const axisScale = React.useMemo(() => [0.88, 0.036, 0.036] as [number, number, number], []);
  const labelColor = React.useMemo(() => getSceneComputedColor("--foreground") || "#111827", []);

  // ...

      <GizmoViewport
        labels={["X", "Z", "-Y"]}
        axisColors={colors}
        axisScale={axisScale}
        axisHeadScale={0.92}
        hideNegativeAxes
        labelColor={labelColor}
        font="16px Inter var, Arial, sans-serif"
```

**Tests:** `compose/ui` — 230 passed; `elements/ui` — 25 passed.

Tracked under ticket **26/04/09/SLIMMER-THREEJS-VIEWPORT-GIZMO** (closed). If you want negative-axis clicks back for ortho snapping, we can re-enable them and still keep thin shafts (e.g. only adjust `axisScale`, not `hideNegativeAxes`).

